# The published tree: every archive built from this repository (an archive of
# a release commit, and a forge's source tarball for a tag) leaves these out.
# They are the private development workflow -- agent instructions, agent
# definitions and working notes -- which name the private forge and internal
# identities. They stay in the private repository. test/releasability enforces
# this list and scans only what it leaves in
# (docs/release/public-releasability.md).
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
AGENTS.md export-ignore
**/.claude/** export-ignore
**/.serena/** export-ignore

# Private-forge and private-release workflow. These files drive only the
# private forge's SDLC -- arming the forge's auto-merge (automerge) -- and the
# private repository's release trust anchor (.release-allowed-signers, which
# pins the internal principal `make release-alpha` verifies against by
# default). Nothing a public reader runs depends on them: ci.yml, release.yml,
# nightly.yml and fuzz.yml neither call nor read them, and a public maintainer
# names their own signers file with RELEASE_ALLOWED_SIGNERS.
.github/workflows/automerge.yml export-ignore
/.release-allowed-signers export-ignore
